# scripts/.env.example
#
# Copy this file to scripts/.env and fill in real values to run the
# release / production-smoke scripts locally. The file is gitignored
# (matches the repo-wide `.env*` rule) and is loaded by
# scripts/lib/load-env.cjs at the top of each script that needs it.
#
# Behavior contract:
#   - If scripts/.env is absent the loader is a no-op (CI's default).
#   - Values in scripts/.env do NOT override variables already set in
#     the environment, so GitHub Actions `env:` blocks always win over
#     any on-disk values.
#   - Scripts that mutate production print a one-line ⚠ banner and pause
#     for ~5s before continuing when their *_SUPABASE_URL points at a
#     non-local host. Pass --yes to skip the pause; CI auto-skips it.
#
# Rotate the service-role key from Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings
# → API at any time; this file is the only place to update locally.

# --- Supabase project (production) ---------------------------------------
# Despite the TEST_ prefix these are the values for the live project the
# scripts mutate. The prefix is historical; renaming is tracked separately.
TEST_SUPABASE_URL=https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co
TEST_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service-role JWT from Supabase dashboard>

# --- Release seed (scripts/release/seed-game-content.cjs) ----------------
# Root-admin auth.users.id used as the published_by audit value on
# game_events / game_content_versions rows the seed inserts.
GAME_SEED_PUBLISHED_BY_USER_ID=<uuid of the publishing admin user>

# --- Production smoke fixtures (scripts/testing/run-production-*.cjs) ----
# The canonical deployed origin the smoke scripts hit — the apps/site
# project, not apps/web. The runners poll `${BASE_URL}/admin` first, and
# `/admin` exists only on apps/site. Pointed at apps/web, the poll takes
# the persistent 404 for deployment propagation and retries to the
# deadline, failing as:
#   Timed out waiting for /admin. Last failure: Unexpected status 404
# The apps/web routes the smoke walks (`/event/:slug/game*`) are reached
# from here through the site → plugin rewrites in apps/site/next.config.ts.
# The two Supabase values below are the publishable (anon) key pair the
# harness uses for unauthenticated fetches, and do mirror apps/web/.env.
PRODUCTION_SMOKE_BASE_URL=https://<your-site-deployment>.vercel.app
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_DEFAULT_KEY=<publishable / anon key>
